<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">arbalist-routes</ansi>

The Arbalist lineage splits at level 10 into a bolt that breaks armor down,
a surer eye that crits through a shield or a warden that sets a pavise for
its row. None of the three asks anything of your alignment, at level 10 or
at level 30. All three shape the Piercing Bolt or the Arbalist's line
(<ansi fg="command">help arbalist</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Siegebreaker</ansi>

  10 Sundering bolts    each bolt that lands takes 10 armor off the foe for the
                        battle, up to 30 (the foe's armor never goes below none)
  15 Heavy stock        a Piercing Bolt deals 20% more damage
  20 Deep sunder        each bolt that lands takes 15 armor off the foe, up to 45
  25 Siege bolts        a Piercing Bolt deals 35% more damage (in all, not on top)

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Siege Master</ansi> (30, still to come): a bolt that passes through to the foe behind.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Sharpshooter</ansi>

  10 Keen sight         +15% critical chance with a shooting weapon, and its
                        critical hits can't be blocked
  15 Steady hands       Steady Aim gives +20 Attack
  20 Practiced loader   the first bolt of each battle needs no winding
  25 Dead eye           +4 Attack with a shooting weapon

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Deadeye</ansi> (30, still to come): a crossbow that is ready again at once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Warden of the Wall</ansi>

  10 Pavise             allies in the Warden's row take 10% less damage, the
                        Warden included (auras don't stack within a row)
  15 Padded coat        +4 armor
  20 Deeper pavise      the row's damage cut is 15%
  25 Wall's keeper      +8% maximum health

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Bastion</ansi> (30, still to come): answers a foe that strikes its column with the
  shot it was holding.

Elite classes are named but not open yet; until they are, an Arbalist keeps
its advanced class's ranks. Routes are final.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help arbalist</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>.
